      "scalar_vs_vector_explanation": "The scalar magnitude regression R^2 evaluates how well predicted displacement magnitude tracks physical displacement magnitude: ||y_hat|| ~ ||y_phys|| via linear regression. In contrast, 2D vector R^2 evaluates variance explained in 2D coordinate space: 1 - sum(||y_phys - y_hat||^2) / sum(||y_phys - mean(y_phys)||^2). Phase 5.1's reported R^2 = 0.2549 for action-conditioned displacement was the scalar magnitude R^2 on clean transitions. In 2D vector space, action displacement explains 43.24% of the displacement variance (R^2 = 0.4324), with component dx R^2 = 0.3107, component dy R^2 = 0.3513, and angular dtheta R^2 = 0.6687.",
