  "mechanistic_conclusion": {
    "scalar_vs_vector_resolution": "Clarified that Phase 5.1's reported displacement R^2 = 0.2549 was computed via scalar magnitude linear regression (||y|| ~ ||y_hat||) on clean transitions. In 2D vector coordinate space, the action-conditioned displacement head achieves R^2 = 0.4324 (dx R^2 = 0.4167, dy R^2 = 0.4579, dtheta R^2 = 0.6802) with translation MAE = 0.0143 m on clean transitions. Learned sensor displacement achieves scalar R^2 = 0.0104 and vector R^2 = -1.9195, confirming that sensor-alone odometry without action guidance has negligible predictive utility.",
    "within_trajectory_shuffling_sensitivity": "Within-trajectory time-shuffled action control permutes the 10 blackout actions across time within each trajectory (50 perms/traj). Action Hold tracking error (0.5490 m) is significantly lower than within-trajectory time-shuffled action hold (0.5565 m, paired delta = -0.0075 m, 95% CI [-0.0115, -0.0036], one-sided Wilcoxon p = 4.078024e-04, sign-flip p = 4.300000e-04). This demonstrates that the ego-motion memory update is sensitive to temporal action order within each individual trajectory, not merely to trajectory-level action distribution statistics."
